{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ESNext",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "lib": ["ESNext", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    // `unplugin-icons/types/solid` is DELIBERATELY ABSENT. It declares
    // `~icons/*` as `(props: ComponentProps<"svg">) => JSX.Element` against
    // `solid-js`, and under Solid 2 `ComponentProps<"svg">` is `never` —
    // core's `ValidComponent` no longer admits a tag name. src/icons.d.ts
    // replaces it; no JSX augmentation can fix the shipped one.
    "types": ["vite/client"],
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "preserve",
    // @solidjs/web, NOT solid-js. Solid 2.0 moved the whole DOM/JSX runtime out
    // of `solid-js` into `@solidjs/web`, and solid-js@2's published `exports`
    // map has no `./jsx-runtime` at all. Leaving this as "solid-js" produces
    // TS2875 ("requires the module path 'solid-js/jsx-runtime' to exist") plus
    // a TS7026 on EVERY intrinsic element, because the JSX namespace is missing
    // rather than wrong — this one line is worth tens of errors on its own.
    "jsxImportSource": "@solidjs/web",
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"],
      "@tlib/shared": ["../../shared/ts/index.ts"],
      "@tlib/shared/*": ["../../shared/ts/*"],

      /* ⚠️ THIS REDIRECT IS WHAT MAKES @ark-ui/solid TYPE-CHECK ON SOLID 2.
         DO NOT REMOVE IT WITHOUT READING src/types/solid-js.d.ts.

         Ark builds EVERY part's props from
         `HTMLProps<E> = JSX.IntrinsicElements[E]`, importing `JSX` from
         `solid-js` — a namespace Solid 2 does not ship. Without it `HTMLProps`
         contributes nothing and every Ark part rejects `class` and `children`,
         which reads as our call sites being wrong and is the namespace being
         empty. Measured here: 144 TS2322s across Dialog, Tabs, Toast, Select,
         Checkbox, Field, RadioGroup and Slider, all from that one absence.

         A `declare module "solid-js"` augmentation (src/solid-1-compat-jsx.d.ts,
         which tCAD, tDetector, tRadio and shared/ts each carry) was tried FIRST
         here and MEASURED NOT TO WORK: an augmentation may only patch
         declarations the target already has, and `solid-js` exports no `JSX`
         whatsoever, so TS accepts it silently and merges nothing. Probed
         directly — `import type { JSX } from "solid-js"` still reports TS2305
         "has no exported member 'JSX'" with that file in the program, and
         `tsc --listFiles` confirms it IS in the program. The same probe reports
         the same thing inside shared/ts, so the augmentation is not carrying
         those trees either; they simply never hand an Ark part `children`.

         This redirect re-exports the real package and adds only the missing
         namespace. Nothing is widened to `any`, so vendor props stay checked.
         It is the arrangement ha-dash already uses, for the same reason.

         Delete this, src/types/solid-js.d.ts and patches/ together when
         @ark-ui/solid publishes Solid 2 types. */
      "solid-js": ["./src/types/solid-js.d.ts"],

      /* Same redirect, for the subpath Solid 2 also stopped shipping.
         `lucide-solid`'s own `types.d.ts` opens with
         `import { JSX } from "solid-js/jsx-runtime"` and builds
         `SVGAttributes = Partial<JSX.SvgSVGAttributes<SVGSVGElement>>` from it,
         so without this `LucideProps` keeps only its eight explicit keys and
         every standard SVG attribute silently disappears. Measured: it surfaced
         as one error on `role` at a single <Dynamic> call site, which reads as
         that call site being wrong rather than as a props type that has lost
         most of itself.

         Our own JSX does NOT go through here — `jsxImportSource` is
         `@solidjs/web` — so this serves vendor declarations only. */
      "solid-js/jsx-runtime": ["./src/types/solid-js.d.ts"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
